note <L003: arithmetic against a neutral element has no effect. A Seed lint rule: it inspects a type-checked binary node and tells a finding when one operand is the identity for the operator. Authored in .tree and loaded by the lint engine as a plugin, with no edit to the engine. The TypeScript original is code/lint/rules/no-redundant-arithmetic.ts.>

load @cluesurf/base/code/rule
  find rule

note <whether an operand is a literal equal to n (a variable has no value field, so it never matches)>

task neutral
  take operand, like dynamic
  take n, like number
  like boolean
  send back
    call is-equal
      read operand/value
      read n

note <the rule the loader reads: a meta object with a spot that tells findings>

task rule
  like rule
  send back
    make rule
      bind name, text <no-redundant-arithmetic>
      bind code, text <L003>
      bind note, text <arithmetic against a neutral element has no effect and should be removed>
      bind spot
        task spot
          take node, like dynamic
          take tell
            like task
              take message, like text
              take span, like dynamic
          fork test
            hook test
              call is-equal
                read node/form
                text <binary>
            hook hold
              save bad, wave false
              fork test
                hook test
                  call is-equal
                    read node/op
                    text <+>
                hook hold
                  save bad
                    call neutral
                      read node/right
                      mark 0
              fork test
                hook test
                  call is-equal
                    read node/op
                    text <*>
                hook hold
                  save bad
                    call neutral
                      read node/right
                      mark 1
              fork test
                hook test, read bad
                hook hold
                  call tell
                    text <this arithmetic has no effect; the result is just the other operand>
                    read node/span
